0..77 Comment "// A fold whose case sits beneath a parameter after the one it recurses on is"
78..156 Comment "// read as the fixpoint, as one with the case at its root is (#2510). Programs"
157..233 Comment "// that only store, quotiented by state\'s put-put law, are folded by passing"
234..313 Comment "// the state: at `Store(s, Store(u, k))` the fold runs to `final(k, u)` through"
314..392 Comment "// two of its own calls, and at `Store(u, k)` through one, so the two sides of"
393..470 Comment "// the law meet from one fresh initial state. The law is the algebraic theory"
471..548 Comment "// of state\'s `put(s, put(u, k)) = put(u, k)` (Plotkin and Power, _Notions of"
549..627 Comment "// computation determine monads_, 2002, doi:10.1007/3-540-45931-6_24), and the"
628..673 Comment "// fold is the handler that passes the state."
675..750 Comment "/// Programs that only store, quotiented by put-put: a store the next store"
751..778 Comment "/// overwrites is no store."
